diff --git a/docs/architecture.md b/docs/architecture.md
index 1c5bdc9..cb8faf1 100644
--- a/docs/architecture.md
+++ b/docs/architecture.md
@@ -163,8 +163,14 @@ rather than using `@work-leaf` read, patch, or lock directives.
 
 - `AgentBackend::launch` starts an agent session from an `AgentLaunch`.
 - `AgentBackend::send` sends a prompt to an existing agent session.
+- `AgentBackend::command` executes a backend-native command, such as a selected-agent slash
+  command, against an existing agent session without sending the text through the normal model
+  prompt path. Providers that do not support backend commands use the default implementation, which
+  returns a visible unsupported-command reply without starting a model turn.
 - `AgentBackend::launch_streaming` and `AgentBackend::send_streaming` provide real-time output to a
   sink of `AgentStreamEvent` values. Their default implementations call the non-streaming methods.
+- `AgentBackend::command_streaming` provides the same command path with optional stream events. Its
+  default implementation calls `AgentBackend::command`.
 - `AgentBackend::launch_streaming_interruptible` and
   `AgentBackend::send_streaming_interruptible` extend the streaming calls with a provider-neutral
   stop detector. Providers that can interrupt an in-flight turn use the detector to stop generation
@@ -187,11 +193,12 @@ then kill to remaining registered processes. This behavior is used by provider i
 spawn real processes.
 
 New agent providers implement `AgentBackend`; they do not add provider logic to `src/codex.rs`.
-Providers that need real-time UI output should override the streaming methods. Providers implemented
-inside this crate can use the crate-private process registration helpers for shared shutdown.
-Providers outside this crate can implement launch, send, and streaming through the public trait; a
-public lifecycle extension is required before external child processes can participate in the shared
-`AgentShutdownHandle` registry.
+Providers that need real-time UI output should override the streaming methods, and providers with
+backend-native command surfaces should override `command` or `command_streaming`. Providers
+implemented inside this crate can use the crate-private process registration helpers for shared
+shutdown. Providers outside this crate can implement launch, send, command, and streaming through
+the public trait; a public lifecycle extension is required before external child processes can
+participate in the shared `AgentShutdownHandle` registry.
 
